<title>USA: Humana to take $0.06/shr Q4 charge.</title>
<headline>Humana to take $0.06/shr Q4 charge.</headline>
<dateline>LOUISVILLE, Ky. 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Humana Inc said Monday it expected to take an after-tex charge of $10 million, or $0.06 per share, in the fourth quarter as it plans to cut nearly 1,000 jobs across the country in 1997.  </p>
<p>Humana said it planned to eliminate about 700 to 900 jobs next year.</p>
<p>It said the reduction in its 18,000-strong work force is a necessary result of its continuing strategic focus on process improvement opportunities, which will enable the company to improve the health of its members and enhance customer service.</p>
<p>Humana is a managed health care company with 4.8 million medical members.</p>
